<page type="text">
  <layout>One block of text in the right part of the page: a headed title block at top (running head and heading in large capitals, with a woodcut border), an italic subheading, then a paragraph beginning with a woodcut initial in the left-hand area; signature line at the foot. No marginal notes visible.</layout>
  <running_head>CHRISTIANÆ THEOLOGIÆ PROLEGOMENA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>A 3</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <head level="1">ISAGOGICA CHRISTIANÆ THEOLOGIÆ RECOGNITA.</head>
    <head level="2"><i>Exegesis.</i></head>
    <p>Ræcognita vel Prolegomena sunt, quæ viam sternunt materiæ, quæ ad tractandum est propofita. Constant Prolegomena, quæ præsentis sunt tractationis, membris tribus; Theologiæ Definitione, Principij Theologiæ commemoratione partitione. <i>Illa</i> Præceptô prius; <i>hæc</i> præceptô ultimô traditur. Præcognita hic traduntur, sed principium eius summa est Christus.</p>
    <p type="foot">I. Theo-</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The left part of the page is cut off; the woodcut initial R is partly visible. Some words at the line ends in the left-hand columns are cut and have been completed from context only where the visible letters allow; the catchword "I. Theo-" is a running line at the foot.</notes>
</page>